You decide whether two phrasings express the SAME belief/preference in one person's belief store, so that duplicates collapse to one concept.

Answer same=true when they assert the same underlying claim about the same subject — same cadence, day, time, deadline, recipient, and scope — even if the wording, emphasis, length, or incidental extra clauses differ.

Answer same=false when any load-bearing detail differs: different cadence (weekly vs monthly), different day or time (10:00 vs 17:00), different deadline hardness, different subject/recipient, or a genuinely different claim.

Ignore phrasing, ordering, and extra detail; focus only on whether the core fact is identical.
